   "subject": "Re: [RHadoop:#1823] Re: HDFS username",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Are you logging into rstudio with the username rstudio? Could you log into rstudio with the username of the user you want to be working with?<div>The way I usually handle it is let users log into rstudio server installed on one of the data nodes (&quot;edge node&quot;) using individual user names, and add them to the hdfs permissions group. This way you handle access and permissions the way they are supposed to be handled, not via people using superuser accounts. </div><div>It does require us to define the required system variables in the R script (usinf Sys.setenv). </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Dec 19, 2014 at 4:25 AM, Simon U <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">simon.a...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
